{
  "_comment": [
    "The status map (docs/gameplay/11_BATTLE_DATA.md §4.2; src/core/game/systems/battle_rules.h): for each fighter's look,",
    "what each status shows: clip (its name in the fighter's .anim; empty: the status's own name), sound (a sound id in",
    "media/sfx) and fx (an effect in media/fx/battle.particle). base: another look whose states this one starts from.",
    "A monster names its look in enemies.json \"look\" (none: \"monster\"); the player's is \"player\".",
    "Statuses: idle, attack, hurt, die, special, transform, parry, broken. A monster's clip is looked up as",
    "<clip>_<monster id> first (its own), then <clip> (monster_battle.anim)."
  ],
  "monster": {
    "states": {
      "idle": {},
      "attack": { "sound": "sfx.enemy_attack" },
      "hurt": {},
      "die": {},
      "special": { "fx": "monster_special" },
      "transform": { "fx": "monster_transform" },
      "parry": { "clip": "hurt", "fx": "monster_parried" },
      "broken": { "clip": "hurt", "fx": "monster_broken" }
    }
  },
  "moss": {
    "base": "monster",
    "character": "anim/monster_moss.anim"
  },
  "hivebear": {
    "base": "monster",
    "character": "anim/monster_hivebear.anim"
  },
